Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1789916399999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789862399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Bar 90's 2771 high with a close 255.7 lower is a buy-climax bar, and the 29 bars since then overlap inside the range rather than trending - trading-range behavior after a climax.", "No close has exceeded 2771; the recent highs 2680 (bar 111) and 2700 (bar 119) are below the spike high, so the range top has already rejected the bulls.", "Bar 115 fell from 2517.53 to 2358.62 in a single bar, showing fast two-sided movement inside the range and poor trend persistence.", "The final bar closed 67.02 below its own 2700 high, so there is no acceptance yet at the upper boundary; the bull push is an in-range leg, not a confirmed breakout.", "The 2357.18 and 2358.62 lows are roughly equal, which marks a range floor that has been tested twice and can break rather than hold."], "evidence_for": ["Net window change is upward (open 2066.43 to close 2632.98) and the post-crash lows rose: 1368.42 (bar 14), 1512.91 (bar 34), 1803.74 (bar 55), 1821.49 (bar 72), 2357.18 (bar 102).", "Bar 88 broke out of a roughly 27-bar consolidation with a 377.29-point range (1905.63-2293.8) closing at 2252.16, and bars 89-90 followed through to 2771, satisfying the breakout-plus-follow-through test.", "Price holds well above the breakout: the last close 2632.98 is about 38% above bar 88's 1905.63 low and has not returned to bar 89's 2111 low.", "The most recent leg is bull: four consecutive higher closes off the 2358.62 double-bottom retest, and bar 119's 2632.98 is the highest close in the supplied window.", "The post-spike range has held above the spike bar's 2325.31 low and keeps making higher swing lows inside the range (2357.18 then 2358.62 with a higher close)."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed D1 bars, open_time 1779494400000 to 1789776000000, with the decision at the close of the final bar (close_time 1789862399999).", "Window high is 2771 (bar 90, open_time 1787270400000); window low is 1368.42 (bar 14, open_time 1780704000000).", "Bars 10-14 (1780358400000-1780704000000) are five overlapping bear bars driving 2006.17 down to 1368.42; bar 14 closes 1568.55, about 200 points above its low, a sell-climax tail.", "Bar 88 (1787097600000) opens 1916.51 inside the prior consolidation and closes 2252.16 near its 2293.8 high; bars 89-90 close 2326.32 and 2515.3, and bar 90 prints 2771 and closes 255.7 below that high.", "Bars 91-119 overlap between 2357.18 (bar 102 low, 1788307200000) and 2700 (bar 119 high); bar 90's low of 2325.31 was never revisited.", "Roughly equal lows at 2357.18 (bar 102) and 2358.62 (bar 115, 1789430400000) form a double bottom at the range low, followed by four higher closes (2416.57, 2446.22, 2612.02, 2632.98).", "The final bar's close 2632.98 is the highest close in the whole window, while its high 2700 stays 71 below bar 90's 2771 high; the last bar closes 67.02 under its own high."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bear leg into a sell climax: bars 0-14 decline from bar 0's 2143.61 high to bar 14's 1368.42 low; the final bars are large bear trend bars and bar 14 closes 200.13 above its low.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779494400000, "upper_boundary": "2143.61"}, {"description": "Two-sided consolidation (bars 61-87, about 27 bars): upper boundary is bar 65's 1974.46 high with repeated 1919-1938 highs; lower boundary is the triple equal low 1821.69/1821.59/1821.49 (bars 70-72). Bar 88 later opened at 1916.51 inside it before breaking out.", "end_time_ms": 1787183999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1821.49", "start_time_ms": 1784764800000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Three-bar bull spike (bars 88-90): 1916.51 to 2252.16 to 2326.32 to a 2515.3 close, with bar 90 reaching 2771 and closing 255.7 off the high - a buy-climax bar.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Post-climax trading range (bars 91-119): upper boundary 2771.00 with internal highs capped at 2557.46, 2537.57, 2680 and 2700; lower boundary 2357.18 (bar 102 low), retested at 2358.62 (bar 115).", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Recent bull leg: four consecutive bull closes from bar 115's 2358.62 low to bar 119's 2700 high; bar 119's close 2632.98 is the highest close of the window.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789430400000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["A close above 2771 followed by a bar holding above 2771 would confirm a bull breakout and move the read toward breakout-spike/channel.", "Rejection at 2700-2771 with a bear close back below 2604.75 keeps the range classification and supports rotation back toward the 2400 area.", "A close below 2357.18 would break the range's double bottom and shift the read toward a range breakdown or deeper bear leg.", "A close below 2111 (bar 89 low) or 1905.63 (bar 88 low) would negate the bull breakout structure and make the bear side the structural read.", "Continued overlapping bars closing between roughly 2400 and 2700 would keep phase as range and Always-In relevance low."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789905599999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: from the 2358.62 low (open 1789488000000) the sequence steps up in both highs and lows into 2700, which is a directional bull leg rather than rotation, and it includes large trend bars at opens 1789732800000 (2507.15 to 2578.60) and 1789747200000 (2579.97 to 2636.28).", "The pullback from 2700 to 2568.16 retraces roughly half of the 2436.87-2700 advance and has not broken the last higher low, which is normal bull-trend behaviour rather than proof of a range top.", "A window high at 2700 following a 2358.62 higher low can also be read as a bull channel inside a wider range, which would put the current pullback in the channel rather than at a range ceiling."], "evidence_for": ["Across 120 bars price repeatedly reversed inside the 2357.18-2700 band: a 2357-2359 double bottom, a 2680 spike that closed 124.48 below its high, a two-sided 2464.27-2609.02 congestion, a 2358.62 retest, and a 2700 probe that closed 61.51 below its high.", "Overlap and reversal count dominate: bodies in the 2464-2609 congestion repeatedly overlap and no more than a few trend bars run consecutively in either direction.", "The 2700 high exceeded the earlier 2680.00 high by only 20 points and closed back inside the prior range, so acceptance above the top is unproven."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars from open_time 1788177600000 to close_time 1789905599999; window high 2700 (bar open 1789804800000) and window low 2357.18 (bar open 1788336000000).", "Two near-equal window lows about 80 bars apart: 2357.18 (open 1788336000000) and 2358.62 (open 1789488000000, close 2412.95).", "Prior spike bar open 1789128000000 ran 2457.12 to a 2680.00 high and closed 2555.52; a later secondary high was 2609.02 (bar open 1789416000000, close 2514.07).", "Latest advance: opens 1789732800000-1789804800000 rose 2507.15 to a 2638.49 close with a 2700 high; that bar closed 61.51 below its high on a 2622.67-2700 range.", "Last three bars closed 2586.68, 2576.90, 2577.8